From 60e252f7bef4cebd8b2d83683ecf77c05665ae76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 06:39:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add shared ai-mode service so every backend uses one Ollama
 integration

Implements the Release 0 shared AI-mode requirement for real: ai-mode/
was previously just a placeholder README saying each backend called
Ollama directly. It's now a running Flask service (ai-mode-service,
port 5099) that is the only thing in the app that talks to Ollama
directly, proxying both the native API (/api/generate, /api/chat,
/api/tags) and the OpenAI-compatible API (/v1/chat/completions,
/v1/models) byte-for-byte.

All five backends (expense-category-tracker, bill-tracker,
student-1-budget, student-5, student-3) are repointed at it via their
existing OLLAMA_URL / OLLAMA_API_URL / OLLAMA_BASE_URL env vars in
docker-compose.yml and docker-compose.student-3.yml. No backend code,
tests, Dockerfile, or CI build step needed to change since the service
mirrors Ollama's own response shape exactly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
